    "created_at": "2024-12-02T09:05:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-12-02T09:05:32Z",
    "body": "Oh I see, that is indeed confusing.\r\n\r\nI was thinking that we probably want to switch `file:` URLs to use opaque hosts instead of domains (for which #599 is the issue) as that would also allow percent-encoding of `@`, for instance and address other issues outlined in #599.\r\n\r\nNow for non-percent-encoded spaces do they need to remain non-percent-encoded or would it be okay when we create the buffer which we pass to the host parser to percent-encode at that point? That way opaque hosts can still ban spaces, but they end up working for `file:` URLs due to preprocessing in the \"file host state\".",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/url/issues/comments/2510953302/reactions",
      "total_count": 0,
      "+1": 0,
      "-1": 0,
      "laugh": 0,
